{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "26", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "12", "M": "53", "S": "50"}}, "news": [{"title": "Garhwa's deputy commissioner orders crackdown on illegal sand mining", "para": "Deputy Commissioner Pashupati Nath Mishra has ordered intensified action against illegal sand mining.  Strict vigil and regular raids will be conducted in specific blocks of Shri Banshidhar Nagar.  Officers must submit updated reports on illegal mining and actions taken.  Coordination between administrative and police officials will be stepped up.  The district administration reiterates its commitment to preventing illegal resource extraction.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/garhwa-deputy-commissioner-launches-major-crackdown-on-illegal-sand-mining/132641507?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-2180500/132641507.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "After eight years of planning, PMRDA\u2019s flagship TP schemes shift to Pune civic body", "para": "Pune Metropolitan Region Development Authority is transferring five town planning schemes to Pune Municipal Corporation. These schemes, including Mhalunge-Maan, were planned for eight years using land pooling. Landowners await promised roads and public amenities after years of waiting. The Pune Municipal Corporation will now oversee the implementation of these projects. Other proposed schemes along the Inner Ring Road face farmer opposition and await policy decisions.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/pune-takes-over-pmrdas-flagship-town-planning-schemes-after-eight-years-of-planning/132641443?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1916225/132641443.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Birla Corporation's profit down 3.2% to \u20b9115.7 crore in Q1 FY27", "para": "Birla Corporation's net profit declined 3.2 percent in the June quarter. Revenue from operations increased 7.8 percent, reaching Rs 2,646.45 crore. Cement sales volume grew five percent, but realization per ton saw a slight increase. The Jute division experienced a revenue drop of 16.7 percent. Cement demand is expected to recover after the monsoon season concludes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/birla-corporation-reports-32-drop-in-q1-fy27-profit-amid-rising-costs/132641185?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-439283/132641185.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}]}